    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics isn't really my thing. I've always struggled with it, especially since I didn't get much formal education. It feels abstract and overwhelming at times, but I respect its importance in other fields like chemistry, which I find more interesting.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, I do. The complexity of math problems often makes me feel anxious, especially if I'm stuck on something for a while. It's not that I can't solve them, but the pressure to understand it quickly adds stress. I prefer subjects where I can see tangible results, like art or cooking.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I haven’t used AI for math learning yet, but I’ve thought about trying it. Since I’m not very comfortable with abstract concepts, tools that break things down step by step or provide visual explanations might help me more than traditional methods.",
